.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.env
# generated PDFs and other runtime output
var/

# Built libswe (Astrodienst source, built by deploy/build-libswe.sh). A build artefact, and
# licensed separately - it must never be committed or reach a publish candidate.
lib/

# THE PROPRIETOR'S OWN WORKING DOCUMENTS AT THE TOP LEVEL, and the scratch scripts beside them.
#
# MATCHED BY SHAPE, NEVER BY NAME. Some of these documents are on the publication exclusion list, and
# published code may not name one - a pointer to a document a stranger cannot open tells them
# something is being withheld and gives them nothing. This file is published like any other, so the
# first version of this block, which listed all eight by filename, was itself the violation: twenty-
# five pointers, found by the proof run over the publish candidate rather than by the suite, because
# the guard read only files with a known text extension and .gitignore has none. Both are fixed.
#
# What this is for: these files were untracked by intention and nothing more, until a bare
# `git add -A` swept six of them into a commit. Untracked-by-intention is a weaker guarantee than it
# sounds, and a test run is too late to be the only thing that notices.
/*.md
!/README.md
/*.sh
